{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/499312-infinite-macabre-changeling-courts-of-the-warp","id":499312,"title":"Infinite Macabre Changeling -- Courts of the Warp","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-01T13:33:03-07:00","id":499312,"title":"Infinite Macabre Changeling -- Courts of the Warp","content":"Okay, so I'm ironically going a little insane here. I really like the idea of the Warp (from Warhammer 40K), and feel like it has potential as a way of explaining Arcadia on a galactic stage. I keep wanting to make courts based around the 4 Chaos Gods, but don't know if that's wise... or logical, given what the Warp would represent in this scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:50:46-07:00","id":499358,"title":"","content":"I guess the Blood God would be an ultra violent mix of the Summer and Dusk court; She who thirsts would be a mix of Spring, the East, and the south courts, The Changer of Ways is Autumn with a lot of talecrafters, Orinmancers and loyalists... I got nothing for Papa Nurgele<br /> <br /> I mean I could work but it would take alot to work I think - It might be better just to pick one aspect of the gods [like just war, sex, magic, family] and make a court based around it instead of trying to the gods themself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar324_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:07:40-07:00","id":499472,"title":"","content":"Theme them after the positive aspects of each Ruinous Power.<br /> <br /> Specifically, Honor, Perfection, Hope and Perseverance. Those seem like things the Damned Courts would come up with if they started from a premise that the world's already gone to Hell, the only point is personal glory and honoring the gods.<br /> <br /> I would also add a punk aspect to the whole thing; the changelings of the Warp are striking out against an evil government by becoming its bogeymen, and as it turns out its bogeymen are those who can live without it. They're not the stooges who march in Black Crusades lead by incompetent Warmasters trying to prove themselves better than their mentor, no; they're the daemons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:25:02-07:00","id":499480,"title":"","content":"Something else:<br /> <br /> I read somewhere that fascist contempt for mental health systems stem from a belief that civilians with trauma haven't &quot;earned' it. They weren't defending the One Just And Proper Way Of Life, so where do they get off, drains on taxes they are?<br /> <br /> I imagine the Imperium, satire it is of fascism in general, agrees. I also imagine changelings get pissed about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:26:03-07:00","id":499481,"title":"","content":"Actually...<br /> <br /> <b>Khorne</b> is the god of <i>action</i>.<br /> <b>Slaanesh</b> is the god of <i>feeling</i>.<br /> <b>Tzeench</b> is the god of <i>change</i>.<br /> <b>Nurgle</b> is the god of <i>stability</i>.<br /> <br /> It's just that the year 40k is <i>so terrible</i> that you only really see their worst aspects (senseless rage and bloodshed, endless depravity and hedonism, pointless change and mad plans, the stagnation of disease).<br /> <br /> Going by that...<br /> <br /> <b>The Khornate Court</b><b>:</b> Their emotion is <i>anger</i>. They treat the Contracts of Bloodshed and Eights as Court Contracts.<br /> <b>The Slaaneshi Court:</b> Their emotion is <i>pleasure</i>. They treat the Contracts of Excess and Sixes as Court Contracts.<br /> <b>The Tzeentchian Court:</b> Their emotion is <i>ambition</i>. They treat the Contracts of Volatility and Nines as Court Contracts.<br /> <b>The Nurglean Court:</b> Their emotion is <i>love</i>. They treat the Contracts of Morbidity and Sevens as Court Contracts.<br /> <br /> If you give me some time, I'll toss in Mantle benefits as well.<br /> <hr /><br /> Of course...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc07.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2011/234/f/e/hwee_prefehr_panceeeeykes_by_mr_culexus-d47fmvx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Sadly, the Hierarch of Anarchy and Terror is no longer canon.<br /> <br /> (<b>The Malicious Court:</b> Their emotion is <i>spite</i>. They treat the Contracts of Anarchy and Elevens as Court Contracts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:39:37-07:00","id":499486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/499312-infinite-macabre-changeling-courts-of-the-warp?p=499481#post499481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually...<br /> <br /> <b>Khorne</b> is the god of <i>action</i>.<br /> <b>Slaanesh</b> is the god of <i>feeling</i>.<br /> <b>Tzeench</b> is the god of <i>change</i>.<br /> <b>Nurgle</b> is the god of <i>stability</i>.<br /> <br /> It's just that the year 40k is <i>so terrible</i> that you only really see their worst aspects (senseless rage and bloodshed, endless depravity and hedonism, pointless change and mad plans, the stagnation of disease).<br /> <br /> Going by that...<br /> <br /> <b>The Khornate Court</b><b>:</b> Their emotion is <i>anger</i>. They treat the Contracts of Bloodshed and Eights as Court Contracts.<br /> <b>The Slaaneshi Court:</b> Their emotion is <i>pleasure</i>. They treat the Contracts of Excess and Sixes as Court Contracts.<br /> <b>The Tzeentchian Court:</b> Their emotion is <i>ambition</i>. They treat the Contracts of Volatility and Nines as Court Contracts.<br /> <b>The Nurglean Court:</b> Their emotion is <i>love</i>. They treat the Contracts of Morbidity and Sevens as Court Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Nurgle is more about despair and entropy, where as Tzeenth is hope/fear of inevitability, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:46:29-07:00","id":499492,"title":"","content":"Nurgle is technically all about ruin, stability, resignation, stagnation, and death.<br /> <br /> Tzeetch is <i>entirely</i> predicated on the idea of being able to change their own destiny. Also Sorcery, Psyker stuff, and the number Nine.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> And the Nurglean Court's emotion is Love because Papa Nurgle <i>lurves</i> everyone! Ah, now I see - you were going for the <i>emotions</i>. Yeah, Despair and Hope <i>might</i> fit better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 05-01-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:56:01-07:00","id":499560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/499312-infinite-macabre-changeling-courts-of-the-wa